Package: argusrm-server
Architecture: any
Depends: libocrpc1, libocsqlite1, libosinfo-bin, osinfo-db, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Description: Argus Remote Manager server
 Argus Remote Manager enrolls managed machines, provides authenticated
 downloads, and coordinates remote management operations. This package
 includes argusrm-controller-cli, the command-line controller that opens
 registration on the server. That command does not use GTK.

Package: argusrm-agent
Architecture: any
Depends: libocrpc1, libocsqlite1, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Replaces: argusrm-agent-cli
Breaks: argusrm-agent-cli
Description: Argus Remote Manager command-line agent
 This package installs the agent on a managed Linux machine. The command
 is argusrm-agent. It does not use GTK. Registration from the command
 line enables and starts its systemd or SysV service. This is the package
 to install on a server.

Package: argusrm-agent-gtk
Architecture: any
Depends: argusrm-agent (= ${binary:Version}), libocrpc1, libocsqlite1, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Description: Argus Remote Manager agent with a registration window
 This package adds the argusrm-agent-gtk command, which opens a desktop
 window for registration, and starts that window at login. The service
 itself is the command-line agent. Install argusrm-agent alone on a
 machine without a desktop.

Package: argusrm-controller
Architecture: any
Depends: libocrpc1, libocsqlite1, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Argus Remote Manager controller
 This package contains the desktop controller. It enrolls with an Argus
 Remote Manager server and opens the management window. Registration on
 the server uses argusrm-controller-cli from the server package.
